## Setting Up a Project

```bash
npm init -y       # creates package.json (project metadata/config file)
npm i express     # install Express framework
```

## What is Express?
Node.js gives us a **runtime** to run JS outside the browser.
But handling every route manually with `if/else` is messy â€” so we use **Express**, a framework on top of Node.js that makes creating HTTP servers and APIs much cleaner.

## JSON â€” How APIs Talk

APIs return data as **JSON** (not HTML). The frontend then uses this data to display whatever it wants.

```json
{
  "queueId": 12,
  "name": "Mess Counter",
  "position": 7,
  "status": "waiting"
}
```
> This is the core idea behind a **REST API**.

## HTTP Methods

| Method | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `GET` | Read data |
| `POST` | Create data |
| `PATCH` | Partially update data |
| `DELETE` | Delete data |

## Middleware

```js
app.use(express.json());
```
A function that **intercepts and processes the request** before it reaches your route handler.
